From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ui/gtk3: show X11 context candidates on the X display

Without an active input-method context, the fallback candidate window is
created as an ordinary Wayland popup with no parent. KWin moves keyboard
focus away from the Xwayland input field when that window is shown, then
IBus clears the preedit on FocusOut. Typing a word only commits a space.

Use the existing X display for that fallback candidate window and its
ordinary X11 positioning path. Keep the input-method Wayland surface for
native text-input clients.

Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
---
--- a/ui/gtk3/candidatepanel.vala
+++ b/ui/gtk3/candidatepanel.vala
@@ -78,6 +78,17 @@
         m_is_wayland = is_wayland;
         m_no_wayland_panel = no_wayland_panel;
         m_toplevel = new Gtk.Window(Gtk.WindowType.POPUP);
+#if ENABLE_XIM && USE_GDK_WAYLAND
+        if (is_wayland && no_wayland_panel) {
+            var display = BindingCommon.get_xdisplay();
+            if (display != null) {
+                // X11 contexts have no parent for a Wayland popup. Use the
+                // X display so showing candidates cannot take their focus.
+                m_toplevel.set_screen(display.get_default_screen());
+                m_is_wayland = false;
+            }
+        }
+#endif
         m_toplevel.add_events(Gdk.EventMask.BUTTON_PRESS_MASK);
         m_toplevel.button_press_event.connect((w, e) => {
             if (e.button != 1 || (e.state & Gdk.ModifierType.CONTROL_MASK) == 0)
